'''''Sedum brissemoretii''''' is a [[flowering plant]] of the genus ''[[Sedum]]'' in the family [[Crassulaceae]] [[endemic]] to [[Madeira]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Sedum brissemoretii Raym.-Hamet |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:275162-1 |access-date=18 October 2024}}</ref> The species is protected under Annex II of the [[Habitats Directive]].<ref name=iucn></ref>

==Distribution and habitat==
''Sedum brissemoretii'' grows in coastal sea cliffs of Madeira.<ref name=iucn></ref>

